      "answer": "a. By the Central Limit Theorem, the sampling distribution is approximately normal; no population-normality assumption is needed for this large sample.\n\nb. $E(\\bar X)=20$ and $\\operatorname{SD}(\\bar X)=4/\\sqrt{64}=0.5$.\n\nc. $z=(21-20)/0.5=2$, so $P(\\bar X>21)=P(Z>2)\\approx0.0228$.\n\nd. $z=(19.385-20)/0.5=-1.23$, so $P(\\bar X<19.385)\\approx0.1093$.",
