      "id": "ch07_q08",
      "answer": "The sampling distribution has mean 50 and standard deviation $5/\\sqrt{100}=0.5$.\n\na. $z=(47-50)/0.5=-6$, so $P(\\bar X<47)\\approx0$.\n\nb. The z-scores are $-6$ and $-1$, so $P(47<\\bar X<49.5)\\approx\\Phi(-1)-\\Phi(-6)\\approx0.1587$.\n\nc. $P(\\bar X>k)=0.35$ means $k$ is the 65th percentile, $z\\approx0.385$. Thus $k=50+0.385(0.5)\\approx50.19$.",
