      "id": "ch07_q10",
      "answer": "a. Label the two employees with 7 days as $7_1$ and $7_2$. The 20 samples are $(1,3,6),(1,3,7_1),(1,3,7_2),(1,3,12),(1,6,7_1),(1,6,7_2),(1,6,12),(1,7_1,7_2),(1,7_1,12),(1,7_2,12),(3,6,7_1),(3,6,7_2),(3,6,12),(3,7_1,7_2),(3,7_1,12),(3,7_2,12),(6,7_1,7_2),(6,7_1,12),(6,7_2,12),(7_1,7_2,12)$. Their sample means have this distribution:\n\n| $\\bar x$ | Frequency | Probability |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| $10/3$ | 1 | $1/20$ |\n| $11/3$ | 2 | $2/20$ |\n| $14/3$ | 2 | $2/20$ |\n| $15/3$ | 1 | $1/20$ |\n| $16/3$ | 3 | $3/20$ |\n| $17/3$ | 1 | $1/20$ |\n| $19/3$ | 1 | $1/20$ |\n| $20/3$ | 3 | $3/20$ |\n| $21/3$ | 1 | $1/20$ |\n| $22/3$ | 2 | $2/20$ |\n| $25/3$ | 2 | $2/20$ |\n| $26/3$ | 1 | $1/20$ |\n\nb. The mean of all sample means is $6$, equal to the population mean $(1+3+6+7+7+12)/6=6$.",
