      "id": "ch07_q11",
      "answer": "a. $\\operatorname{SD}(\\bar X)=2/\\sqrt{25}=0.4$.\n\nb. $P(7.8<\\bar X<8.2)=P(-0.5<Z<0.5)\\approx0.3829$.\n\nc. For $n=100$, SD $=0.2$, so the z-scores are $-1$ and $1$ and the probability is $0.6827$.\n\nd. The larger sample has a smaller standard error, so more means fall near 8.\n\\ne. The three probabilities are $P(X>11)=P(Z>1.5)=0.0668$, $P(\\bar X_{25}>9)=P(Z>2.5)=0.0062$, and $P(\\bar X_{100}>8.6)=P(Z>3)=0.00135$. Thus the single session is most likely, followed by the 25-session mean, then the 100-session mean.",
