    {
      "id": "rotel_ch07_sampling_mean_01",
      "answer": "a. Since $\\operatorname{SD}(\\bar X)=\\sigma/\\sqrt n$, $\\operatorname{SD}_{84}/\\operatorname{SD}_{42}=\\sqrt{42/84}=1/\\sqrt2$; it decreases by a factor of $\\sqrt2$.\n\nb. $E(\\bar X)=\\mu=5.95$ ounces for either sample size, so it does not change.\n\nc. No. Because the population is normal, the sample mean is exactly normal for either sample size; the CLT is not needed.",
