      "id": "ch07_q22",
      "answer": "Use $\\bar x\\pm t_{\\alpha/2,n-1}s/\\sqrt n$ when $\\sigma$ is unknown and the data are a random, independent sample of a quantitative variable. For small $n$, the population should be approximately normal with no strong outliers; for larger $n$, the CLT provides robustness.",
