      "id": "opl_nau_ch07_clt_01",
      "answer": "For a sample proportion, standard error is proportional to $1/\\sqrt n$. Therefore,\n\n$$\\frac{0.05}{0.02}=\\sqrt{\\frac{n_2}{100}}.$$\n\nSquaring gives\n\n$$n_2=100\\left(\\frac{0.05}{0.02}\\right)^2=100(6.25)=625.$$\n\nThe required sample size is **625**.",
