      "answer": "a. The sampling distribution has\n\n$$\\mu_{\\bar X}=\\mu=120$$\n\nand\n\n$$\\sigma_{\\bar X}=\\frac{\\sigma}{\\sqrt n}=\\frac{30}{\\sqrt{36}}=5.$$\n\nb. Standardizing,\n\n$$z=\\frac{130-120}{5}=2.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$P(\\bar X>130)=1-\\Phi(2)=1-0.97725=0.02275\\approx0.0228.$$",
